{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>נודי</b> — like נדודי (my wanderings); and he dwelt in the land of Nod." "<b>ספרת</b> — the meaning: You know how many times I wander from my place, and it is a figurative expression, נודי עם בנאדך (my wanderings are with your people [?]). And the meaning: for his drops, which are his tears, are counted by HaShem. And this is the meaning of הלא בספרתך — as though they are strung in a flask, by way of parable, so that not a drop of them is lost."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 56, :notes {1 "The phrase נודי עם בנאדך is opaque; read here hyper-literally. Possibly corrupt or elliptical."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:32:01.743852175Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}